---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Send an exchange's request again, with secrets read from the store now

Usage: rustman history replay [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          The exchange id (or a unique prefix of it)

Options:
      --no-history
          Do not record the replayed exchange

      --body-only
          Print only the response body: a text body redacted (unless --show-secrets), a binary one byte for byte

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write the response body, byte for byte, to FILE instead of stdout

      --show-secrets
          Print secret values and credential headers as they are, on this terminal only (history and reports stay redacted)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards; outside any workspace, the ad-hoc history)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
